1
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:04,960
Josuke, I'm going on a hunting trip. Huh?

2
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:07,074
And you're coming too.

3
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:10,110
Whoa there!

4
00:00:10,193 --> 00:00:11,337
Hang on a second, Jojoro!

5
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,557
Run that by me again!

6
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,337
I could have sworn you
said we were going hunting!

7
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:16,250
If...

8
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:17,163
that's true...

9
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:21,457
Does that mean we're going hunting
for hotties with hot bodies?

10
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,137
Cause you should know, I'm a
little more the romantic type.

11
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:26,057
I'm not sure I'll be able to pull it off.

12
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:28,081
You'll have to show me the ropes.

13
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:30,820
I spoke to Otoishi. He confessed.

14
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:32,380
Are you serious?

15
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,682
Yeah, he had quite a lot to say.

16
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,317
Especially regarding the bow and arrow.

17
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,857
It turns out he also
used it to shoot a rat.

18
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:40,770
He did what?

19
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:42,540
That's right.

20
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,280
But the rat didn't die.

21
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:46,397
Even though it was writhing in agony,

22
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:50,127
it freed itself from the arrow
and made a break for the hills.

23
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,111
You know what that means.

24
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:57,677
Humans aren't the only organisms with
the potential to acquire stand abilities.

25
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:59,917
But we don't know what this rat can do,

26
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,840
so we have to hunt it
down before it lashes out.

27
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:11,737
I'll see you

28
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:18,820
soon.

29
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:29,657
That was awesome.

30
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:31,977
Those were just regular cans.

31
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:34,777
Keeping a nimble rat within
range won't be so easy.

32
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:36,697
Which is why we have these bearings.

33
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:38,777
They'll expand your range to 20 meters.

34
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,297
This should be obvious.

35
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:42,237
But they're useless against stands.

36
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:45,555
Use them when you're in
position to take down the user.

37
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:46,537
Give it a try.

38
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:47,897
I have to use them too.

39
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:50,397
You sure about this?

40
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,157
I don't even have the concentration.

41
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:54,600
for ball sports and stuff, you know?

42
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,560
Oh, I almost got it.

43
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,540
Not bad for a newbie.

44
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,779
I'd give it an 85.

45
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:16,317
But I need you to remember
one thing while on this hunt.

46
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:21,200
When dealing with live animals, you
have to prioritize composure over speed.

47
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,857
If you corner the rat
and screw up the shot,

48
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:28,417
don't expect it to be gullible
enough to come within range again.

49
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,777
So hold your fire until you
know you can hit your target.

50
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:34,657
One more thing, don't let
the pressure bog you down.

51
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:35,570
Got it?

52
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:39,380
Well, he sure knows how to
make a guy feel at ease.

53
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:45,660
From what he told me, Otoishi shot
the rat near this irrigation canal.

54
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:49,520
Given the location, it
was probably a brown rat.

55
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,885
Brown rats are agile swimmers.

56
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:54,769
Adaptable and can eat
practically anything.

57
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:58,258
Larger rats can grow up to
20 or 30 centimeters long.

58
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:00,737
And some can weigh as much as one kilogram

59
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:03,349
with a horizontal leap
of about two meters.

60
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,940
Found them. Huh?

61
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,997
You mean those aren't bird tracks?

62
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:11,256
Its four feet have four
digits and its hind feet five.

63
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:14,011
The S shape means it's dragging something.

64
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:16,024
These markings are tail tracks.

65
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:18,500
The rat's about 20 centimeters long.

66
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:22,174
I don't know how many, but
there are more than one here.

67
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:27,131
There's a tick on this leaf, which means
it's a stomping ground for rodents.

68
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:30,126
There's no question about it.

69
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:32,300
Somewhere in that drain is a nest.

70
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:38,308
For now, our best bet is to set a trap
and see what the video camera picks up.

71
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:43,668
That's one of those cameras that lets
you watch while you're recording, right?

72
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:47,228
You're not going to use
cheese for the trap?

73
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:49,157
It's a hunk of tempura.

74
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:52,020
Cheese is too luxurious for a common rat.

75
00:04:57,620 --> 00:04:59,149
What's with all the flies?

76
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:00,519
Did something die?

77
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,150
Jojaro!

78
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:04,160
These are...

79
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:12,100
Those are dead rats!

80
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:13,780
Yeah, no shit!

81
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:16,880
Oh, it looks like a block of jellyfish!

82
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:22,140
Why the hell are you poking it?

83
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:23,400
It's flesh.

84
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:28,222
At some point, the flesh of these
rats melted and later congealed.

85
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:31,877
It seems as though the melting
started from under their flesh.

86
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:36,220
How in the world does something as
messed up as that even happen? Dunno.

87
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:41,237
If I had to guess, I'd say this is
the handiwork of the rat we're after.

88
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,700
So it stand at this?

89
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:44,640
That seems to be the case.

90
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:49,096
It took out its fellow rats to seize
the territory, which would mean...

91
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:52,593
It's highly likely the rat's
making a nest in that drain.

92
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:57,440
The question now is, has our culprit
used its powers to wreak any more havoc?

93
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:08,033
Looks like the drainage canal
continues on to that house.

94
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:10,200
It might already be too late.

95
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,129
You think it beat us here?

96
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:15,515
At first glance, I see a
chicken coop, but no chickens.

97
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,453
The cars are still parked in the garage.

98
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:21,677
and there doesn't appear to
be any activity in that house.

99
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:23,878
The front door is unlocked and open.

100
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:27,413
All signs point to the rat being inside.

101
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:31,637
It's safe to assume the owners of
this house have already been killed.

102
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:32,550
Let's go.

103
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:34,200
We have to investigate.

104
00:06:43,260 --> 00:06:45,977
The rat will let us approach
it up to a certain point.

105
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:50,157
It's intelligent enough to know that most
humans are too slow to ever catch it.

106
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:53,340
So it's not expecting to
be used as target practice.

107
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:58,300
That's how we'll close in and put
an end to this mess with one shot.

108
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:00,450
Bingo.

109
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:02,612
These are rat droppings.

110
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,257
There's no grass or grain here.

111
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:07,500
Only meat.

112
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:12,060
The droppings lead to
that room. Come on. Right.

113
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:24,010
What?

114
00:07:24,093 --> 00:07:26,387
It looks like an old
refrigerator compressor.

115
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:29,820
What the hell?

116
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:33,728
Am I going crazy or did the
refrigerator just open by itself?

117
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:36,668
Did the door's magnet
give out or something?

118
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,340
Holy shit, I found it!

119
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:40,997
That little bastard's right there!

120
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:42,400
I get it.

121
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:44,437
So that's what opened the fridge.

122
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:47,197
Nobody told me rats could
open refrigerator doors.

123
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:48,927
That doesn't make any sense.

124
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:51,640
Someone must have
forgotten to shut it. No.

125
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:52,940
Get real, Josuke.

126
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,077
You're not that gullible, are you?

127
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:56,940
This rat's a stand user.

128
00:07:58,760 --> 00:07:59,590
Jo...

129
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:01,430
That's right.

130
00:08:01,513 --> 00:08:04,420
Jotaro went into the next
room to look for the rat.

131
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:11,360
Freaking great now our eyes have met

132
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:18,500
How the hell the rat did this

133
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:25,117
They're still alive did
the rat disfigure the

134
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,317
owners of this house with
its stand so it have An

135
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:31,257
easier time storing them
in the fridge oh and

136
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:35,160
it's eating them damn it
Jotaro's not coming back!

137
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:37,558
I'll have to kill this thing myself!

138
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:42,373
When dealing with live animals, you
have to focus on composure over speed.

139
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:46,314
If I don't tag him on my first
try, he'll know my range.

140
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:47,841
Damn it, Jotaro!

141
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:50,880
I know you said no pressure, but still...

142
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:55,477
Of course, the table and chair are
positioned just enough to be in my way.

143
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:59,917
I have to make sure I sink this ball
bearing right between his beady little eyes.

144
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,080
Now, stay right there.

145
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:04,370
Oh, crap!

146
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,659
He stopped eating!

147
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:08,219
If I move closer, he'll run for it!

148
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:09,950
Forget this!

149
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:11,037
It's now or never!

150
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:12,885
I'll blast him from over here!

151
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:15,420
He's moving! Now!

152
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:19,860
I got him!

153
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:23,846
Shit, it wasn't a fatal blow!

154
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:27,200
Here we go!

155
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:29,539
That weird machine must be a stand!

156
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:34,377
Alright, pal, come and get some if you
think you've got what it takes to beat me!

157
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:37,931
Just know that my next shot is
gonna take you out for good.

158
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:40,655
Damn it, he's running under the table!

159
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:42,720
No, you don't!

160
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,457
Jotaro, what the hell are you doing?

161
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:48,680
The rat's in here!

162
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:56,740
That shape...

163
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:58,130
Not good!

164
00:09:58,260 --> 00:09:59,907
His stand fires projectiles!

165
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:04,210
What now?

166
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:06,457
Should I slap it away with my bare hands?

167
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:08,080
No, that's disgusting!

168
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:10,701
Where's the rat?

169
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:13,804
Did I hit it with my ball
bearing or did I miss?

170
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,140
You bastard!

171
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:22,230
Yeah!

172
00:10:22,313 --> 00:10:23,476
I got him after all!

173
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:27,457
It wasn't between his eyes like
I said, but he's still a goner.

174
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:28,775
That was a close one.

175
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,100
Hey, Jotaro!

176
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:32,190
Get over here!

177
00:10:32,273 --> 00:10:34,020
I took out the rat!

178
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,380
The hunt is over!

179
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:39,477
Jeez, what were you doing in there?

180
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:41,857
You went missing right
when I needed you the most.

181
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,417
I was starting to think
you'd abandoned me.

182
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:46,400
But hey, at least it's dead.

183
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:48,837
Luckily, everything
went according to plan.

184
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:49,877
Well, for me, that is.

185
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:52,019
Our rat friend wasn't so fortunate.

186
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:55,399
Though his stand shot some
needle-like things at me.

187
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:59,965
Whatever they were, I bet they're
what turned your flesh to goo.

188
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:03,677
He got to the people who own this
place, but they're still alive.

189
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:06,348
I'll fix them right up
with Shining Diamond.

190
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:11,319
If we don't eliminate them by sundown,
things might get even messier.

191
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:12,490
Huh?

192
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:16,036
There was another rat, and
that one managed to hit me.

193
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:19,126
Jotaro, your hand is melting!

194
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,017
It happened in the other room.

195
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,924
I could have dodged the attack.

196
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:27,081
But I thought catching the needle
for analysis was the best choice.

197
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:30,157
All it takes is a touch
and it stands poison

198
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:33,100
begins to permeate even
melting other stands.

199
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:38,277
Five or six hits and you'll turn
into a quivering mass of flesh.

200
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:41,677
Oh good thing that needle didn't hit me.

201
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:44,937
Never thought I'd be
grateful for being squeamish.

202
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:48,497
The rat bolted out the door
after hitting me with the needle.

203
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:51,997
Somehow it must have figured out you
killed its kin here in the kitchen.

204
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:56,857
Um sorry to bother but would you
mind using your power to fix my hand?

205
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:59,077
Not to worry, just leave it to me.

206
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,617
Damn it.

207
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:03,420
Why those little SOBs have to multiply?

208
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:15,397
This is the Speedwagon
Foundation Research Department.

209
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:17,837
Hello, this is Jotaro.

210
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:18,861
Jokujo speaking.

211
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:20,280
Jotaro, finally!

212
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:22,657
We've tried to reach you several times.

213
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:25,277
I was hunting the rat
and had the ringer off.

214
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:26,740
Is this about Otoishi?

215
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:28,870
Yes.

216
00:12:28,953 --> 00:12:32,677
Akira Otoishi was withholding the fact
that he shot two rats instead of one.

217
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:33,590
Are you sure?

218
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:36,377
Is there any chance he could
have shot three or four?

219
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:37,290
No, sir.

220
00:12:37,373 --> 00:12:38,376
We're sure it's two.

221
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:41,560
Oh, good grief, Otoishi.

222
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:45,060
What a fool.

223
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:50,797
When it comes to its own territory, it'll
kill everything, humans and rats alike.

224
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:52,660
It cares only about itself.

225
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:58,000
So, this savage's time on Earth is
about to come to a fast end. Let's move.

226
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,657
Jotaro, hold on a minute, would you?

227
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:03,680
A pint-sized rodent just
ran into an open field.

228
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:06,837
How exactly do you plan on
tracking this thing down?

229
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:09,861
A famous artist, Ernest
Thompson Seton, once said,

230
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:12,897
There's not an animal on the
planet that cannot be tracked.

231
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:14,860
You have to know their habits.

232
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,572
Rats are known to avoid unfamiliar paths,

233
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:22,389
which means its root of escape had to
be that irrigation channel from before.

234
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:25,997
And there's something else about rats.

235
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:30,080
If they're not constantly eating,
they'll starve within a few hours.

236
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:32,830
There.

237
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,588
Those are fresh bite marks.

238
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:35,800
Nice going!

239
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:37,571
This is an awesome start!

240
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:40,426
Now we're gonna corner
that bucktooth bastard!

241
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:44,837
Take a look at this I don't think he even

242
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:48,660
gave a damn that our bait
was here he's on tape

243
00:13:56,980 --> 00:14:01,800
Huh his ear looks like a bug-eaten leaf
what do you say we call him bug-eaten

244
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:07,157
He's being cautious this isn't
gonna be like at the house bug-eaten

245
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:10,817
is gonna be extra careful to not let
us skip within 20 meters of them.

246
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:13,057
We'll have to use these to finish the job.

247
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:14,600
Wait, those are real?

248
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:16,214
Yeah, they have to be.

249
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:20,519
Because of air resistance, ball
bearings lose accuracy when traveling

250
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:21,517
over 20 meters.

251
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:26,365
With a bullet nose like this, we'll be
able to hit our mark up to 70 meters away.

252
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:29,277
Will I have to launch that
with my stand's hand too?

253
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:32,301
Because I don't think I'm
ready for that just yet.

254
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:34,000
Point taken.

255
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:36,341
I'll have to be the one to do it.

256
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:40,600
Hold it right there.

257
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:43,397
Just what are you trying to say?

258
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:45,656
That comment didn't sit well with me.

259
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:50,437
I am the one who nailed the rat
back at the house, remember?

260
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:53,277
Sure, it wasn't exactly a
perfect shot, but still.

261
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:55,140
Guess you're right. Take two.

262
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:02,900
More pressure.

263
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:36,500
Be careful.

264
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:39,020
This puddle is full of leeches. What?

265
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:47,750
Shit.

266
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,260
So what's going on?

267
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:51,620
Be careful. Eyes up.

268
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:54,320
The footprints suddenly stop here.

269
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,652
You've got to be joking!

270
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:59,214
Why would they randomly stop like that?

271
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:00,850
I know.

272
00:16:00,933 --> 00:16:01,763
He's under us.

273
00:16:01,846 --> 00:16:03,737
He must have burrowed a
hole and covered himself.

274
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:04,650
No.

275
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:07,067
This is called backtracking.

276
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:09,655
I didn't know rats could do this, too.

277
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:10,950
Backtracking?

278
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:13,917
Backtracking is the way
in which a wild animal

279
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,557
reverses itself by
stepping in its own tracks.

280
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:19,557
This confuses predators long
enough for them to hide.

281
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:24,157
In Japan, the behavior has been observed
with brown bears, weasels, and rabbits.

282
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:27,475
However, it is unheard of
among rats and other rodents.

283
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:31,017
Okay, so let me get this straight.

284
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:34,747
You're saying that a common brown
rat pulled a fast one on us?

285
00:16:35,100 --> 00:16:37,297
Things have taken a turn for the worse.

286
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:41,439
With this kind of terrain, the
hunters may have just become the prey.

287
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:46,237
I have this creepy feeling
we're being watched.

288
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:49,117
We better duck behind a rock
while we still have the chance.

289
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:50,440
No sudden movements.

290
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:56,337
The good news is Bug Eaton's attack
isn't too fast for us to see.

291
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:58,517
Just keep an eye out
for the point of fire.

292
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:02,365
If we can figure out where he's
hiding, we'll snipe him instead.

293
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:11,500
Son of a bitch!

294
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:20,740
That dirty rodent used our
own rat trap against us?

295
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:24,380
Star Platinum, the world!

296
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:27,340
Oh, good grief.

297
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:37,437
Don't worry I removed the
needle before the poison

298
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:40,777
spread along with all
the affected tissue you

299
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:45,017
should put a bandage on it
I was also able to locate

300
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:48,457
his general whereabouts
take a look he's halfway

301
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:53,037
up the hill near those
three rocks you found him

302
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,477
and helped me I don't know
who's more amazing you

303
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:58,037
are the rat compared with
the two of you I'm starting

304
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:00,885
to feel like I'm a kid
at the Grown-up's table.

305
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,560
It's 60 meters away.

306
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,118
So far, no sign of any more needles.

307
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:13,317
He knows a random firing
would give away his location,

308
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:16,137
and it's obvious he doesn't
want to be attacked.

309
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:17,740
He's a stubborn bastard.

310
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:20,139
Why are you praising that damn rat?

311
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:23,032
We need to act, and we have to do it now.

312
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:25,260
Well spoken, Josuke.

313
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:28,617
We need to give this assault
everything we've got.

314
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:30,900
or Bug-Eaten will kill us both.

315
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:34,020
All right, I'll give you all four rounds.

316
00:18:36,420 --> 00:18:37,620
At this distance,

317
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:42,353
the rounds will rise like sliders, so
aim one centimeter below the target.

318
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:46,900
If I'm firing, what are you going to do?

319
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,492
I'm moving in so he'll shoot his needles.

320
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:53,220
Your job, Josuke, is to
determine his location.

321
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:56,520
Then, I'm counting on you to end this.

322
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,220
You want me to what?

323
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:01,915
You don't have a choice in the matter.

324
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:07,600
Even if one or two of his needles get me,

325
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:10,408
you can just use Shining
Diamond to heal me.

326
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:15,642
You can't heal yourself with that
power, so you get the kill shot.

327
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:23,677
This is our last stand.

328
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:24,590
Make it count.

329
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:30,121
Could I have a second to prepare?

330
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:33,000
Star Platinum! The world!

331
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,260
Did you find him? No.

332
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:48,697
As soon as he fired, he ran
off and hit somewhere else.

333
00:19:48,780 --> 00:19:52,309
I'll try getting closer while
going up the side of the hill.

334
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:53,880
Wait for him to fire.

335
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:55,460
Yeah, will do.

336
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:57,640
Damn this pressure.

337
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,620
There! I see him!

338
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,177
What the...

339
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:13,357
That little shit-heel
predicted I'd dodge his

340
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:15,877
attack and fired the needles
at the rocks instead.

341
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,340
They ricocheted at me.

342
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:24,850
Jotaro, no!

343
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:27,477
Don't stand there gawking at me, Josuke!

344
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,117
Keep your eyes trained on the rat.

345
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:31,857
The moment he attacks, blow
his ass straight to hell!

346
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:32,917
This isn't good.

347
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,647
I've got four rounds,
but I'm out of chances.

348
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,877
If I waste even a single second?

349
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:40,280
Here we go, Josuke.

350
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:45,950
There!

351
00:20:46,033 --> 00:20:50,404
He's in the same spot as the last time he
fired, but he's hiding behind the rocks.

352
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:51,730
Shit!

353
00:20:51,813 --> 00:20:53,681
If only he was looking over here!

354
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,180
I've gotta do this.

355
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,297
I'll just have to hit a tiny target.

356
00:21:01,380 --> 00:21:02,280
No problem.

357
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:07,260
I suddenly feel that fighting spirit.

358
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:09,776
Right then, it's time for you to die.

359
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:21,240
Shosuke Mists!

360
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,740
What do we do now?

361
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:33,760
There you are.

362
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:36,517
I knew my Mists would
make you turn around.

363
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,540
It's good to see that ugly face.

364
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:42,960
And right now, you're
right in my crosshairs.

365
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:59,266
Guess I can hang with
the grown-ups after all.

366
00:21:59,820 --> 00:22:04,200
Call me Josuke Higashikata, the mighty
vanquisher of pressure and stress.

367
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:07,457
Akira's mutant stand rats got me thinking.

368
00:22:07,540 --> 00:22:10,217
They are reflections of our
destruction of the environment.

369
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:11,771
I'm not sure how to feel.

370
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:14,873
But at least Josuke is a dependable guy.

371
00:22:15,580 --> 00:22:16,640
Good grief.

372
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:19,865
Maybe now we'll all get
a little peace of mind.

373
00:22:46,060 --> 00:22:48,517
Anytime I need to see a
face, I just close my eyes.

374
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:50,717
And I am taking two
bits with crystal mine.

375
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:52,537
And magenta, feeling me take a shelter.

376
00:22:52,620 --> 00:22:54,937
In the face of my spine, straight
like a Chaka cherry cola.

377
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:57,537
I don't need to try to
explain, I just hold on tight.

378
00:22:57,620 --> 00:22:59,877
And if it happens again,
I'ma move so slightly.

379
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:03,617
To the arms and the lips and the face
Of the human kind of all that I need to,

380
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:04,530
I want to.

381
00:23:04,613 --> 00:23:06,317
Come and stand a little bit closer.

382
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:08,557
Breathe in and get a bit higher.

383
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:13,037
You'll never know what
hit you when I get to you?

384
00:23:13,120 --> 00:23:18,200
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you, but ooh,

385
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,480
I've got to find out.

386
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:22,810
Ooh,

387
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:29,520
I want you, I don't know if I need
you, but ooh, I've got to find out.
